{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107391","id":2583156216,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6Z99X4","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107391","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107391.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107391.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107391","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107391/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107391/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107391/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/eeac57075ce473fb1c7e51de02c912d8f7882f58","number":107391,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"OpenXR: Add support for spatial entities extension","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"[The OpenXR Spatial entities extension](https://www.khronos.org/blog/openxr-spatial-entities-extensions-released-for-developer-feedback) was introduced to standardise obtaining and interacting with information about the users real world environment.\r\n\r\nIt defines [a core extension](https://registry.khronos.org/OpenXR/specs/1.1/html/xrspec.html#XR_EXT_spatial_entity) for how to query and interact with spatial entities, and defines additional extensions that detail out specific uses of these entities.\r\n\r\nCurrently the core specification has support for:\r\n- [Spatial anchors](https://registry.khronos.org/OpenXR/specs/1.1/html/xrspec.html#XR_EXT_spatial_anchor), this supports marking locations in the real world that can be made persistent. Ideal for placing virtual objects into the real world and having them reconstructed in future sessions\r\n- [Plane tracking](https://registry.khronos.org/OpenXR/specs/1.1/html/xrspec.html#XR_EXT_spatial_plane_tracking), identifies various surfaces such as floors, walls, tables, etc. This allows us to know where surfaces are and provides the ability to place/attach virtual objects on/to these surfaces or apply physics to these surfaces.\r\n- [Marker tracking](https://registry.khronos.org/OpenXR/specs/1.1/html/xrspec.html#XR_EXT_spatial_marker_tracking), visually detects markers in the real world and brings their position into the virtual world. Currently supported are QR codes, Aruca markers or April tags.\r\n\r\nThe spatial entities system is designed to be incredibly modular with future plans for additional (vendor) extensions to unlock further functionality. The core of the implementation in Godot therefor exposes a fair amount of underlying features that can be used in GDExtension plugins to implement such extensions or for users to fully customize the setup.\r\n\r\nHowever, in plain vanila mode all this logic comes built in and can be enabled in project settings. Using the built in logic all spatial entities are recorded as Anchor trackers with the XR Server and can be consumed through a simple manager script.\r\n\r\nWhile the implementation is deemed complete based on the published specification, runtime implementations are still being worked upon and some tweaking will be expected.\r\n\r\nDocumentation can be found here: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-docs/pull/11015\r\nDemo project can be found here: https://github.com/BastiaanOlij/spatial-entities-demo\r\n\r\nFor testing sadly there are no public runtime implementations yet, however myself, David and Fredia have access to betas and have tested this.\r\n\r\n*Contributed by Khronos Group through the Godot Integration Project*","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":865585000,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4NjU1ODUwMDA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:xr","name":"topic:xr","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12939969,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AxXLB","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/23","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23/labels","number":23,"state":"closed","title":"4.6","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions